|name2 = Mega Shark vs. The White Hare
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Mega Shark vs. The White Hare''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Like the other [[Ancient Heroes ULTRA SOULS (Gacha Event)|ULTRA SOULS]], Hare of Inaba has significantly different stats between Normal (spammable) and Evolved Form (high performance), both of which can be used effectively depending on the situation.

==='''Normal Form'''===
Hare of Inaba's stats are stupidly high for such a stackable attacker. Each one averages a DPS of ~6,311 against targets at Lv.30 (~10,023 DPS at Lv.50), which is to say having multiple out on the field has the potential to completely eviscerate everything in sight. This is further complemented by [[Shortened Cooldown]] cutting its recharge by 50% every two deployments, leaving it with an effective recharge rate of 8.4 seconds. They're also very healthy, so healthy in fact that their effective HP surpasses that of an equal level [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] (148,500 vs. 141,750 EHP at Lv.50). Inaba is not too prone to getting overwhelmed by sheer numbers thanks to its stats. Even in the face of an army, it doesn't particularly matter when they're the ones marching directly into shark-infested waters. With respectable speed and standing range, they can infiltrate blind spots relatively easily and even sneak in hits on enemies that naturally outrange them. Tired of strategizing? [[Cruel Angel Clionel]] got you down? The solution can be as simple as spamming them and letting them do their work.

The main thing to be wary of with Inaba is untargeted supports. They're a fish out of water without their high stats doing the heavy lifting, and high-range attackers can wipe out your entire stack of them in mere seconds if you're not careful. Moreover, they lack immunities to debuffs outside of [[Special Abilities#Immune to Weaken|Weaken Immune]], so they can be perma-stunned by Slow/Freeze/Warp, or potentially disabled by Curse. Remember, Inaba is not cheap, and each set of two costs 1,950¢, which can take its toll if you're not consistently making those benjamins fly. Regardless, Inaba is a fantastic unit who handily shuts down a majority of Angels and Aliens.

==='''Evolved Form'''===
You'll be using this Uber in sets of two, as Shortened Cooldown cuts its recharge by 75% every two deployments. With that in mind, Mega Shark vs. The White Hare covers the bases that Hare of Inaba struggles with, having a higher standing range and being more well-equipped for longevity in stages where short-ranged attackers don't work nearly as well, such as [[Glass Slippers]] or [[AI Fishing]]. It has insanely high burst damage through semi-frequent [[Special Abilities#Savage Blow|Savage Blows]], hitting for upwards of 201,960 DPH against targets at Lv.30, and maintaining an average DPS of ~15,353 (320,760 Savage Blow DPH and ~24,385 DPS at Lv.50). Just like its Normal Form, these numbers are obscenely high given how fast it attacks and the fact that there's usually going to be two of them on the field at any given moment. It's unlikely the first will die before the second one recharges either, since they have an effective HP of 233,750 at Lv.30 (371,250 EHP at Lv.50) and a knockback count of 4; its high mobility further aids its versatility, and it comes with all the advantages of a rebound attacker. Within its targets, there's almost nothing that can withstand the relentless assault from two of these monsters, and even against untargeted supports, its base stats hold up well enough to make it through most encounters. Mind your wallet if you plan on using Mega Shark vs. The White Hare, as 9,300¢ is not a light investment.

