==Trivia==
*Hare of Inaba is based on the Japanese myth of the [[wikipedia:White Hare of Inaba|White Hare of Inaba]], who tries to cross the ocean by convincing many sharks to form a line under the pretense of wanting to count how many members the shark clan has compared to the hare clan. As he nears the end of the bridge the sharks unwittingly formed for him, the hare enrages them by boasting about how he tricked them, causing the last shark to attack and rip his fur off. The black-haired cat accompanying the hare in this unit's design most likely represents the hare's savior, [[wikipedia:Ōkuninushi|Ōkuninushi]], who helps the hare recover his fur by advising him to wash himself in fresh water and then roll in the pollen of cattail grass.
*The "Mega Shark" is likely a reference to the [[wikipedia:Megalodon|Megalodon]].
*Along with [[Thunder God Zeus (Uber Rare Cat)|Almighty Zeus]], they are the very first units with Shortened Cooldown ability.
**In Almighty Zeus' case, he gain Shortened Cooldown ability through [[Talents|Ultra Talents]].

